
==============================================================================
22.1 Phasor Maxwell, true or false
==============================================================================
  [(a) curl E~ = -j w mu H~, curl H~ = (sigma + j w eps) E~ on a damped wave] phasor Faraday rel.res 2.2e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell (sigma + j w eps) 2.2e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  [(b) d rho/dt at t = 1.10e-07: finite difference -1.051374e+07 = Re(+j w rho~ e^jwt) -1.051374e+07] OK
  [(b) d rho/dt at t = 3.70e-07: finite difference -6.209205e+06 = Re(+j w rho~ e^jwt) -6.209205e+06] OK
  [(b) d rho/dt at t = 8.30e-07: finite difference 8.731112e+06 = Re(+j w rho~ e^jwt) 8.731112e+06] OK
  (b) so continuity is div J~ + j w rho~ = 0, i.e. div J~ = -j w rho~ (statement's +j w rho~ is FALSE)
  [(c) div D~ (with D~ from Ampere-Maxwell) equals rho~ = -div J~/(j w): max rel. dev. 6.0e-07] OK
  (d) sigma + j w eps = 0.100000 +0.000556j S/m (nonzero) -> rho~ = 0 for any field strength
  (d) relaxation time eps/sigma = 8.8419e-10 s = 0.884 ns (exact eps0: 0.885 ns); period at 1 MHz = 1.0 us; ratio period/(eps/sigma) = 1131
  [(d) sigma + j w eps != 0] OK
  (e) sigma/(w eps0) = 1800.0000 (course eps0) / 1797.5 (exact eps0) -> eps_c/eps0 = 10 - j1800
  [(e) j w eps_c = sigma + j w eps] OK
  (e) sigma/(w eps) = 180.0  (conduction current 180 x displacement current)
  (f) angle of sigma (conduction current / E): 0.0 deg; angle of j w eps (displacement / E): 90.0 deg -> conduction in phase, displacement leads by 90 deg (statement reversed: FALSE)
  ANSWER 22.1: (a) T (b) F (c) T (d) F (e) T (f) F

==============================================================================
22.2 Which phasors are allowed (gamma^2 = -8 + j6 1/m^2)
==============================================================================
  principal sqrt(-8 + 6j) = 1.0000 +3.0000j  (1 + j3), |gamma| = sqrt(10) = 3.1623
  [(1 + 3j)^2 = -8 + 6j] OK
  (a) x 2e^{-(1+3j)z}              lap/E = -8.0000 +6.0000j (need -8+6j: yes); div E = 0.00e+00 (0) -> ALLOWED
  (b) y 2e^{+(1+3j)z}              lap/E = -8.0000 +6.0000j (need -8+6j: yes); div E = 0.00e+00 (0) -> ALLOWED
  (c) x 2e^{-(3+j)z}               lap/E = 8.0000 +6.0000j (need -8+6j: NO); div E = 0.00e+00 (0) -> not allowed
  (d) x 2e^{-(1-3j)z}              lap/E = -8.0000 -6.0000j (need -8+6j: NO); div E = 0.00e+00 (0) -> not allowed
  (e) z 2e^{-(1+3j)z}              lap/E = -8.0000 +6.0000j (need -8+6j: yes); div E = 4.37e+00 (NONZERO) -> not allowed
  (f) x 2e^{-(1+3j)(0.6y+0.8z)}    lap/E = -8.0000 +6.0000j (need -8+6j: yes); div E = 0.00e+00 (0) -> ALLOWED
  (c) (3+j)^2 = (8+6j); (d) (1-3j)^2 = (-8-6j); (f) 0.6^2 + 0.8^2 = 1.00
  (d) e^{-(1-3j)z} = e^{-z} e^{+j3z}: phase says travel -z, amplitude grows toward -z (grows along its travel)
  (e) div E~ = dEz/dz = -gamma Ez != 0
  [22.2 key = (a), (b), (f)] OK
  medium with this gamma^2 at w = 3e8, mu0: sigma + j w eps = 0.015915 +0.021221j (sigma = 1/(20 pi) = 0.015915, eps = 8.000 eps0); eta = 119.2151 e^(j18.43 deg)
  [22.2 (a) with H~ = u x E~/eta] phasor Faraday rel.res 1.7e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell (sigma + j w eps) 1.7e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  [22.2 (b) with H~ = u x E~/eta] phasor Faraday rel.res 1.7e-10 | Ampere-Maxwell (sigma + j w eps) 1.7e-10 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  [22.2 (f) with H~ = u x E~/eta] phasor Faraday rel.res 9.3e-11 | Ampere-Maxwell (sigma + j w eps) 9.2e-11 | div/curl 2.5e-11 -> OK

==============================================================================
22.3 Reading a damped wave: E = x 20 e^{-0.5z} cos(2pi 1e8 t - 2pi z + 45deg) V/m
==============================================================================
  travel: opposite signs on t and z -> +z; e^(-0.5 z) decays toward +z (consistent)
  omega = 6.2832e+08 rad/s, f = 100.0 MHz, alpha = 0.5 Np/m, beta = 6.2832 rad/m
  gamma = 0.5000 +6.2832j 1/m = 6.3030 e^(j85.45 deg) 1/m
  lambda = 2pi/beta = 1.0000 m, v_p = w/beta = 1.0000e+08 m/s, delta = 1/alpha = 2.0 m
  e^-2 = 0.13534, e^-4 = 0.01832
  at z = 4 m: amplitude 20 e^-2 = 2.7067 V/m (13.53 %), power fraction e^-4 = 0.01832 (1.83 %)
  per wavelength the amplitude is multiplied by e^(-alpha lambda) = e^-0.5 = 0.6065
  alpha/beta = 0.0796 -> tau = 4.55 deg, sigma/(w eps) = 2ab/(b^2-a^2) = 0.1602
  (for reference, eps of a non-magnetic medium with this gamma: (b^2-a^2)/(w^2 mu0) = 8.943 eps0)
  [22.3 E] page's time-domain formula vs Re(phasor e^jwt): max rel. dev. 2.7e-15 (tol 1e-12) -> OK

==============================================================================
22.4 Possible or not possible
==============================================================================
  scan sigma/(w eps) from 1e-6 to 1e8: max alpha/beta = tan tau = 0.99999999 (< 1), max tau = 45.000000 deg (< 45)
  (a) alpha/beta = 2/0.5 = 4 > 1 -> NOT POSSIBLE
  [(a) beta >= alpha always] OK
  (b) w eps = 2 pi 1e9 * 4e-9/(36 pi) = 0.2222 S/m (= 8/36)
  (b) sigma/(w eps) = 0.045000 (course eps0; = 9/200) / 0.04494 (exact) -> imperfect dielectric
  (b) exact alpha = 0.94224 Np/m, beta = 41.8985 rad/m, alpha/beta = 0.02249
  (b) shortcuts: (sigma/2)sqrt(mu/eps) = 0.9425 Np/m, w sqrt(mu eps) = 41.8879 rad/m
  [(b) alpha << beta] OK
  (c) 2 ns at 50 MHz = 36.0 deg; H lags E by tau >= 0, so a lead is NOT POSSIBLE; the largest possible lag is 45 deg = 2.50 ns
  (d) delta = lambda/10 -> alpha lambda = 10 -> alpha/beta = 10/(2 pi) = 1.5915 > 1 -> NOT POSSIBLE; min delta/lambda over the scan = 0.159155 -> 1/(2 pi) = 0.159155
  (d) good-conductor limit: per wavelength e^(-2 pi) = 0.00187 (0.19 %)
  [(d) delta >= lambda/(2 pi)] OK
  (e) plasma N = 1e11 m^-3: f_p = 2.839 MHz (9 sqrt(N) = 2.846 MHz)
  (e) at 2 MHz: sigma = 0.00000000 -0.00022424j S/m (purely imaginary), gamma = 0.042239 +0.000000j 1/m (real), delta = 23.68 m, eta = 0.000 +373.861j Ohm (purely imaginary)
  [(e) plasma: sqrt((wp^2 - w^2))/c = gamma] OK
  (e) <S> at z = 3 m: brute [ 0.00000000e+00  0.00000000e+00 -4.05797603e-20] formula [0. 0. 0.] W/m^2 (zero); Re(sigma) = 0.0 -> no Joule heating
  [(e) <S> = 0 below cutoff] OK
  ANSWER 22.4: (a) NP (b) P (c) NP (d) NP (e) P

