22.5 Find the error: E = z 60 e^{-ax} cos(wt - bx), travel +x, eta = 150 e^{j20 deg} Ohm
==============================================================================
  u x E-hat = x x z = -y; H~(0) = [ 0.        +0.j         -0.37587705+0.13680806j  0.        +0.j        ] -> |H| = 0.400 A/m, phase -20.0 deg relative to -y
  correct: H = -y 0.4 e^{-ax} cos(wt - bx - 20deg) A/m (H lags E by 20 deg); student: +20 deg (leads)
  test medium: w = 1e8, mu0 -> gamma = 0.2865 +0.7872j (|gamma| = 0.8378, angle 70 deg); sigma + j w eps = gamma/eta = 0.003590 +0.004278j (Re > 0: passive)
  [22.5 corrected H] phasor Faraday rel.res 2.5e-11 | Ampere-Maxwell (sigma + j w eps) 2.3e-11 | div/curl 0.0e+00 -> OK
  student's H in Faraday's law: rel. residual 0.684 (fails)
  [22.5 student's H fails Faraday] OK
  <S> at x = 0 with the correct H: brute 11.2763 x-hat, formula 11.2763 W/m^2
  <S> at x = 0 with the student H: brute 11.2763 x-hat, formula 11.2763 W/m^2
  1/2 * 60 * 0.4 * cos 20 = 11.2763 W/m^2 for both -> power cannot detect the slip
  a lead (tau = -20 deg) would need sigma/(w eps) = tan(-40 deg) = -0.839 < 0 (active medium)

